==Trivia==
*Like [[Bakoo]], she is based on the ''[[wikipedia:Baku (mythology)|Baku]]'', a Japanese mythical creature that devours dreams.
**The Japanese term ''baku'' can also refer to a [[wikipedia:Malayan tapir|Malayan tapir]], which Bakoo closely resembles. Doremi, being entirely white, looks like an [https://www.nationalgeographic.com/adventure/article/150321-tapirs-albinos-brazil-animals-science-rare albino lowland tapir].
*Her gender is confirmed by her Korean name, Doremi Yang (도레미양), which can be taken as "Miss Doremi". When attached to a name, 양 ''yang'' is used for a girl or young woman, especially of lower age than the speaker; the masculine equivalent is 군 ''gun''.
*Doremi's name may be derived from:
**The "do-re-mi" syllables of the sol-fa scale.
**"[https://youtu.be/dpVhzTivUZo Do Re Mi Fa Daijōbu]", a song by [[wikipedia:B.B. Queens|B.B.Queens]] used as the opening theme for [[wikipedia:Old Enough!|''Old Enough!'']]. In Japanese, both [[Baby Fake (Merciless)|First Errand]] and ''Old Enough!'' are named ''Hajimete no Otsukai'' ("My First Errand"), except First Errand is はじめてのお使い while ''Old Enough!'' is はじめてのおつかい.
**[https://en.touhouwiki.net/wiki/Doremy_Sweet Doremy Sweet] from the bullet hell game [[wikipedia:Touhou Project|''Touhou Project'']], who is also a ''Baku''.
**''[[wikipedia:Ojamajo Doremi|Ojamajo Doremi]]'', a magical girl anime aimed at young girls.
*Based on her Japanese description and Slow ability, Doremi may have been inspired by the ''[[wikipedia:Anpanman|Anpanman]]'' character [[wikia:anpanman:Kokin-chan|Kokin-chan]], a childish young girl who was introduced as an antagonist and mastered crocodile tears, crying to get her way and force others to cry, which usually immobilizes them similarly to how Doremi nearly immobilizes cats.
*Her attack animation may take inspiration from the [https://www.pikminwiki.com/Fiery_Blowhog Fiery Blowhog] from the ''[[wikipedia:Pikmin|Pikmin]]'' series.
*Among the Tier 2 [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], Doremi may represent the virtue of humility, as she remains a humble baby rather than trying to be or appear as anything more.
*She can be seen as a foil to her original variant: Bakoo is a perpetual sleepwalker whereas Doremi's cries put others to sleep.
*Her English description misspells the word "unconscious" as "unconcious".
*She is tied with Bakoo for the shortest standing range and longest reach of any Advent Boss.

